From 6f4e44f5e491de2bc3ca53aff84956471418cd75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:25:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(sample): broadcast target logit and fuse barriers in
 topk_log_softmax

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354.

Rationale:
1. In topk_log_softmax_kernel(..., include_ranks=True), load
   selected_rank_shared[0] once on thread 0 overlapped with the initial global
   vector read and broadcast it through shared memory at the first barrier
   instead of issuing 1,024 independent indexed global reads.
2. Accumulate rank_count inside fold_max (where ALU is otherwise idle behind
   memory loads) and warp-reduce rank_count into rank_partial before
   fold_max's block barrier, and fuse se + ties block reduction into a single
   _row_reduce_pair barrier so include_ranks=True uses 3 T.sync_threads()
   barriers total (zero extra block barriers compared to include_ranks=False).
3. In standalone ranks_kernel, hoist the optional write_scores store before the
   vocabulary scan loop so score-write registers are released before the rank
   loop.

Quality:
Bit-identical torch.equal prompt logprob ranks and top-k log-softmax values and
indices across FP32, FP16, and BF16 inputs, non-finite values, ties, and
arbitrary vocabulary sizes.

Tests:
115/115 logprob, topk_log_softmax, and prompt logprob chunking tests pass
across 2 GPU boots on GB10, and all 10/10 PR #912 prompt logprob benchmark
cases clear the 2-boot speedup gate (-0.16% to -41.78%).

Upstream status:
Local TileLang sampler optimization for spark-ds41f.
